        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 1,
            "column": 3
          },
          "text": "Ionic and Capacitor live updates with @capgo/capacitor-updater"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 3,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 3,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "@capgo/capacitor-updater is the open-source updater plugin behind Capgo live updates for Ionic and Capacitor apps. It downloads approved web bundles, applies them with native rollback protection, and keeps binary-only changes on the normal App Store and Play review path."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 5,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 5,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Use it when you need OTA updates for HTML, CSS, JavaScript, assets, and other web-layer changes after your native shell is already approved."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": {
        "line": 7,
        "column": 1
      },
      "depth": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 7,
            "column": 4
          },
          "text": "Install"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "location": {
        "line": 9,
        "column": 1
      },
      "lang": "bash",
      "meta": null,
      "text": "npm install @capgo/capacitor-updater\nnpx cap sync"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": {
        "line": 14,
        "column": 1
      },
      "depth": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 14,
            "column": 4
          },
          "text": "Where It Fits"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 16,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 16,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "For Ionic teams, live updates usually mean the same workflow: ship a new web bundle without forcing every user through a full store release. Capgo handles that workflow for Capacitor apps with channels, compatibility checks, rollout control, device logs, and rollback."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 18,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 18,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Native plugins, entitlements, Android manifest changes, iOS plist changes, and binary SDK updates still require a normal app store release. Keep those changes in your native build pipeline and use live updates for the approved web layer."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
